From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(GameLaunchMenu): L1 and R1 show the game before or
 after

On a game's page (Play Now and the controller, settings and delete
buttons; opened with A on the game's card) the way to another game was
Back, the D-pad to its card and A again. L1 and R1 did nothing there:
they are the tab actions, which only the library's tab header handles.

They now show the game before (L1) or after (R1) the one on the page,
in the row or grid the page was opened from: Home's recent games, or a
library tab, OpenGamepadUI's own or a plugin's. The order is the one
the cards are laid out in, so the end of a grid's row is followed by
the start of the next. Past the first or the last game nothing happens;
Home's Library card is no game, and cards a search has hidden are
passed over (game_beside.gd). The list is the one a card of the game is
on screen in as the page opens, and it is kept through the game's
settings and back. The page leaves L1 and R1 alone while a menu is open
over it, while one of its install dialogs is open, and with Guide held.

Back then puts the focus on the card of the game last shown: the
library would return to the card the page was opened from, and Home to
its first card. The page defers that twice, so that it comes after the
list's own choice, which the list defers as its state is entered. Back
without L1 or R1 is as before.

The bottom bar names the two buttons on that page: "Previous" with
L1's icon and "Next" with R1's, after Accept and Back, each only while
there is a game that way, so the first game of a row shows Next alone.
The page tells the bar (its group, show_game_steps()) each time it shows
a game and as it is left. The bar shows and hides a box around each
InputIcon, since an InputIcon makes itself visible again whenever the
kind of input changes.

The page's logo and banner load in two awaited steps, and two games'
loads can now overlap: art that arrives for a game no longer shown is
dropped.

The library's tab header fades out for a moment after the library is
left and still took L1 and R1 meanwhile: R1 pressed 60 ms after a card
opened its page changed the library's tab behind the page (MANGMI Air X,
2026-11-27). Its input now stops as the library is left.

On that device, with its own buttons: from Home, A on Stardew Valley,
then R1, R1, L1 showed Among Us, Megabonk and Among Us again, and Back
put the focus on Among Us's card; L1 on the first game and R1 on the
last of the nine did nothing. From All Games, A on the sixth card, the
last of its row, then R1 twice showed the seventh and the eighth, and
Back put the focus on the eighth; in the grid R1 and L1 changed tab as
before. From the RetroForge plugin's Steam tab likewise. A and R1 60 ms
apart showed the next game and left the tab alone. The bottom bar had
Next alone on the first game of Home's row, Previous and Next on the
second, Previous alone on the ninth and last, neither in the game's
settings, both again back on its page, and neither on Home or in the
library.
---
diff --git a/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd b/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
index e3b7e91..0aeff10 100644
--- a/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
+++ b/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
@@ -16,8 +16,15 @@ var game_settings_state := preload("res://assets/state/states/game_settings.tres
 var gamepad_settings_state := preload("res://assets/state/states/gamepad_settings.tres") as State
 var logger := Log.get_logger("GameLaunchMenu")
 
+const GameBeside := preload("res://core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_beside.gd")
+
 @export var launch_item: LibraryLaunchItem
 
+## The row or grid the page was opened from, and the game it was opened on: L1 and R1 show the
+## game before or after the one shown (_input).
+var _list: Node
+var _opened: LibraryItem
+
 @onready var banner := $%BannerTexture as TextureRect
 @onready var logo := $%LogoTexture as TextureRect
 @onready var launch_button := $%LaunchButton as CardButton
@@ -34,6 +41,7 @@ var logger := Log.get_logger("GameLaunchMenu")
 # Called when the node enters the scene tree for the first time.
 func _ready() -> void:
 	set_process(false)
+	set_process_input(false)
 	launcher_state.state_entered.connect(_on_state_entered)
 	launcher_state.state_exited.connect(_on_state_exited)
 	launch_button.button_up.connect(_on_launch)
@@ -55,6 +63,57 @@ func _process(_delta: float) -> void:
 
 
 func _on_state_entered(_from: State) -> void:
+	set_process_input(true)
+	_note_list()
+	_show_game()
+
+
+## The row or grid the page is opened from is the one a card of its game is on screen in: that
+## list is still shown as the page opens. Back from the game's settings none is, and the list
+## found before stays while it has the game.
+func _note_list() -> void:
+	var item := launcher_state.data.get("item") as LibraryItem
+	if not item:
+		_list = null
+		return
+	for card: GameCard in get_tree().get_nodes_in_group(GameCard.GROUP):
+		if card.library_item == item and card.is_visible_in_tree():
+			_list = card.get_parent()
+			_opened = item
+			return
+	if is_instance_valid(_list) and not GameBeside.card_of(_list.get_children(), item):
+		_list = null
+
+
+## L1 and R1 show the game before or after this one in the row or grid the page was opened from,
+## in the order its cards are laid out, and do nothing past its ends.
+func _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
+	var step := int(event.is_action_pressed("ogui_tab_right")) - int(event.is_action_pressed("ogui_tab_left"))
+	if step == 0 or Input.is_action_pressed("ogui_guide") or not is_instance_valid(_list):
+		return
+	# Not under a menu opened over the page, nor while one of its dialogs is open
+	var focus := get_viewport().gui_get_focus_owner()
+	if not focus or not is_ancestor_of(focus) or location_menu.visible or options_menu.visible:
+		return
+	var card := GameBeside.beside(_list.get_children(), launcher_state.data.get("item"), step) as GameCard
+	if not card:
+		return
+	get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
+	launcher_state.data = {"item": card.library_item}
+	_show_game()
+
+
+## The bottom bar names L1 and R1, each while it has a game to show (none once the page is left).
+func _hint_steps(on_page: bool) -> void:
+	var nodes: Array = _list.get_children() if on_page and is_instance_valid(_list) else []
+	var item := launcher_state.data.get("item") as LibraryItem
+	get_tree().call_group("context_bar", "show_game_steps",
+		GameBeside.beside(nodes, item, -1) != null, GameBeside.beside(nodes, item, 1) != null)
+
+
+## Sets the page up for the game in the launcher state's data
+func _show_game() -> void:
+	_hint_steps(true)
 	# Fade in the banner texture
 	player.play("fade_in")
 
@@ -105,10 +164,15 @@ func _on_state_entered(_from: State) -> void:
 	var logo_texture = await (
 		BoxArtManager.get_boxart_or_placeholder(library_item, BoxArtProvider.LAYOUT.LOGO)
 	)
+	# Another game may be shown by now (L1/R1): its own load sets the art
+	if launcher_state.data.get("item") != library_item:
+		return
 	logo.texture = logo_texture
 	var banner_texture = await (
 		BoxArtManager.get_boxart_or_placeholder(library_item, BoxArtProvider.LAYOUT.BANNER)
 	)
+	if launcher_state.data.get("item") != library_item:
+		return
 	banner.texture = banner_texture
 
 	loading.visible = false
@@ -120,6 +184,19 @@ func _on_state_exited(to: State) -> void:
 	if to == in_game_state:
 		state_machine.remove_state(launcher_state)
 	set_process(false)
+	set_process_input(false)
+	_hint_steps(false)
+	# Back at the list on another game than the one it opened: that game's card takes the focus,
+	# after the list's own choice (Home's first card, the library's last focused one), which the
+	# list defers as its state is entered. Hence deferred twice.
+	var item := launcher_state.data.get("item") as LibraryItem
+	if item != _opened and is_instance_valid(_list):
+		_focus_card.call_deferred(GameBeside.card_of(_list.get_children(), item))
+
+
+func _focus_card(card: Control) -> void:
+	if is_instance_valid(card) and card.is_visible_in_tree():
+		card.grab_focus.call_deferred()
 
 
 func _update_launch_button() -> void:
diff --git a/core/ui/card_ui/navigation/context_bar_menu.gd b/core/ui/card_ui/navigation/context_bar_menu.gd
